      "writtenOn": "2023-12-08T17:45:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I think ideally we could do a few combinations here:\n\n```\n// Format: BGRA8, Surface: kRGB_888x, Data: kBRGA_888x\n{\n    auto\u0026 ioFormat \u003d ctInfo.fExternalIOFormats[ioIdx++];\n    ioFormat.fColorType \u003d GrColorType::kBGR_888x;\n    ioFormat.fExternalType \u003d GR_GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE;\n    ioFormat.fExternalTexImageFormat \u003d GR_GL_BGRA;\n    ioFormat.fExternalReadFormat \u003d \n        formatWorkarounds.fDisallowBGRA8ReadPixels ? 0 : GR_GL_BGRA;\n}\n```\n\nor\n\n```\n// Format: BGRA8, Surface: kRGB_888x, Data: kRGBA_888x\n{\n    auto\u0026 ioFormat \u003d ctInfo.fExternalIOFormats[ioIdx++];\n    ioFormat.fColorType \u003d GrColorType::kRGB_888x;\n    ioFormat.fExternalType \u003d GR_GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE;\n    ioFormat.fExternalTexImageFormat \u003d GR_GL_RGBA;\n    ioFormat.fExternalReadFormat \u003d GR_GL_RGBA;\n}\n```\n\nNow today I only the second option actually works because we don\u0027t have a BGR_888x colorType right now. However, we do want to add that colorType to simplify things. Though I think if we really did have the colorType we\u0027d end up more with something like the following and drop the RGB_888x versions:\n\n```\n// Format: BGRA8, Surface: kBGR_888x\n{\nauto\u0026 ctInfo \u003d info.fColorTypeInfos[ctIdx++];\nctInfo.fColorType \u003d GrColorType::kBGR_888x;\nctInfo.fFlags \u003d ColorTypeInfo::kUploadData_Flag;\nctInfo.fReadSwizzle \u003d skgpu::Swizzle::RGB1();\n// Format: BGRA8, Surface: kBGR_888x, Data: kBRGA_888x\n\n{\n    auto\u0026 ioFormat \u003d ctInfo.fExternalIOFormats[ioIdx++];\n    ioFormat.fColorType \u003d GrColorType::kBGR_888x;\n    ioFormat.fExternalType \u003d GR_GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE;\n    ioFormat.fExternalTexImageFormat \u003d GR_GL_BGRA;\n    ioFormat.fExternalReadFormat \u003d \n        formatWorkarounds.fDisallowBGRA8ReadPixels ? 0 : GR_GL_BGRA;\n}\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "c07f5b94_a741df5f",
